    "v2_flexible_UFPbM8": {
      "type": "v2_flexible",
      "blocks": {
        "headline_xHiKaw": {
          "type": "headline",
          "settings": {
            "heading_text": "<p>Key Responsibilities of a Nutrition Coach</p>",
            "heading_align": "left",
            "heading_width": "full",
            "heading_type": "h3",
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "heading_no_decal": false,
            "heading_decal_left": true,
            "heading_strong_accented": false
          }
        },
        "subheadline_Vnhqbt": {
          "type": "subheadline",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>As a <strong>Nutrition Coach</strong>, your role goes beyond simply giving advice. You’ll work closely with clients to understand their lifestyle, guide their decision-making, and support long-term, sustainable change. </p><p></p><p>Your responsibilities typically include: <br/></p>",
            "text_align": "left",
            "text_width": "full",
            "text_size": "copy-l",
            "text_no_decal": false,
            "text_strong_accented": false,
            "margin_top": 16,
            "margin_bottom": 0
          }
        },
        "textcol_7kaeFQ": {
          "type": "textcol",
          "settings": {
            "left_text": "<p></p><p><strong>Client Assessments</strong><br/><br/>Understanding a client’s current habits is the foundation of effective coaching. This involves reviewing food intake, lifestyle factors, and personal goals to build a clear picture of where they are starting from.<br/><strong><br/>Education & Coaching</strong><br/><br/>A key part of the role is helping clients understand nutrition in a practical way. This includes explaining concepts like calories, macronutrients, and portion control so they can make informed decisions independently.<br/><br/><strong>Scope of Practice Management</strong><br/><br/>As a Nutrition Coach, it’s essential to work within your professional boundaries. This means supporting generally healthy individuals and referring clients with medical conditions to qualified healthcare professionals where appropriate.<br/></p>",
            "left_text_size": "copy-l",
            "left_text_no_decal": false,
            "left_text_strong_accented": false,
            "right_text": "<p></p><p><strong>Nutrition Planning</strong></p><p></p><p>Based on your assessment, you’ll create structured, personalised nutrition strategies tailored to each client’s goals - whether that’s fat loss, muscle gain, or improved performance.</p><p><br/><br/><strong>Progress Monitoring</strong></p><p></p><p>Tracking progress allows you to adjust strategies over time. This may involve reviewing body composition, performance, or adherence to ensure clients stay on track.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Maintaining Professional Standards</strong></p><p></p><p>To build a sustainable career, you’ll need to stay up to date with industry knowledge, maintain insurance, and continue developing your skills through ongoing education.<br/><br/></p><p></p>",
            "right_text_size": "copy-l",
            "right_text_no_decal": false,
            "right_text_strong_accented": false,
            "margin_top": 0,
            "margin_bottom": 0
          }
        },
        "subheadline_LfcfkB": {
          "type": "subheadline",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p></p><p><strong>Key Skills Involved:</strong> Communication, Nutrition Knowledge, Behaviour Change, Empathy, Problem Solving, Assessment, Goal Setting, Organisation, Adaptability etc.</p>",
            "text_align": "left",
            "text_width": "full",
            "text_size": "copy-l",
            "text_no_decal": false,
            "text_strong_accented": false,
            "margin_top": 0,
            "margin_bottom": 0
          }
        }
      },
