    "v2_accordion_QgWf3B": {
      "type": "v2_accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "accordion_row_NTEyk8": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What qualification do I need to become a Gym Instructor in the UK?",
            "row_content": "<p>To work as a <strong>gym instructor in the UK</strong>, you need a <strong>Level 2 Certificate in Fitness Instruction</strong> that is Ofqual-regulated and endorsed by CIMSPA. No degree required – just commitment and a passion for fitness. </p><p>This qualification provides the knowledge and practical skills required to work safely on the gym floor, including exercise technique, programme design, and health and safety procedures. </p><p>Once qualified, you will be eligible to apply for <strong>gym instructor jobs in commercial gyms, leisure centres, and health clubs</strong>. </p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_w94eBY": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do I need prior experience to start a Level 2 course?",
            "row_content": "<p>No - A <strong>Level 2 Gym Instructor course</strong> is designed for beginners who want to start a career in the fitness industry. </p><p>You do not need previous gym employment or fitness qualifications to enrol - just a passion for fitness and a commitment to learning.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_gjjh3n": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long does it take to qualify? ",
            "row_content": "<p>The time it takes to qualify as a gym instructor depends on the course format and study schedule. </p><p>Most learners complete their <strong>Level 2 Gym Instructor qualification</strong> within: </p><ul><li><strong>4–8 weeks</strong> for intensive courses </li><li><strong>2–4 months</strong> with flexible study options </li></ul><p>Study Active offers flexible learning so you can complete your course at a pace that suits your lifestyle. </p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_h7qVTJ": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I study the Gym Instructor course online? ",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes - We at Study Active offer <strong>blended learning options</strong> for gym instructor qualifications. </p><p>This usually includes: </p><ul><li>Online theory modules </li><li>Practical workshops and assessments </li></ul><p>Blended learning allows you to gain both the <strong>theoretical knowledge and practical coaching experience</strong> required to work confidently in a gym. </p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_AXjDyG": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do I need insurance to work as a Gym Instructor? ",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes - Most gyms require instructors to have <strong>public liability insurance</strong> before working with members. </p><p>This insurance protects both you and your clients while delivering fitness guidance. Once you have completed your qualification, you will be able to apply for insurance through specialist fitness insurance providers. <br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_DkqUqw": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is the difference between a Gym Instructor and a Personal Trainer? ",
            "row_content": "<p>A <strong>Gym Instructor (Level 2)</strong> typically works on the gym floor supporting members by: </p><ul><li>Delivering gym inductions </li><li>Demonstrating exercise technique </li><li>Writing basic gym programmes </li></ul><p>A <strong>Personal Trainer (Level 3)</strong> works more closely with individual clients and usually: </p><ul><li>Delivers one-to-one coaching sessions </li><li>Designs advanced training programmes </li><li>Charges clients per session </li></ul><p>Most fitness professionals start as gym instructors before progressing to <strong>Level 3 Personal Training</strong>. </p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_CMxgmy": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I progress to Personal Training after Level 2? ",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes. Completing a <strong>Level 2 Gym Instructor qualification</strong> allows you to progress to a <strong>Level 3 Diploma in Personal Training</strong>. </p><p>This qualification enables you to work as a personal trainer, train clients one-to-one, and increase your earning potential within the fitness industry. </p><p>An alternative is to complete the <a href=\"https://studyactive.co.uk/products/cimspa-endorsed-level-3-diploma-practitioner-in-personal-training\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Level 2 and Level 3 in one comprehensive course</span></a>. <br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_Ra8WMq": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What jobs can I apply for after qualifying? ",
            "row_content": "<p>After completing your <strong>Level 2 Gym Instructor qualification</strong>, you can apply for roles such as: </p><ul><li>Gym Instructor </li><li>Fitness Instructor </li><li>Leisure Centre Fitness Staff </li><li>Health Club Assistant </li></ul><p>Many instructors use this role to gain experience before progressing to <strong>personal training or specialist fitness careers</strong>. </p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_iFRxiJ": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is the Gym Instructor qualification recognised internationally?",
            "row_content": "<p>CIMSPA-endorsed and Ofqual-regulated qualifications (like Study Active's) are highly regarded in the UK and often accepted abroad (e.g., Europe, UAE via eREPs equivalents). For full international work, check local requirements, but our certification provides a strong global foundation.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_pExgKk": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do I need to be a member of CIMSPA or REPs?",
            "row_content": "<p>CIMSPA membership isn't mandatory to work as a PT, but it's highly beneficial for CPD, professional standards, job listings, and credibility. REPs (legacy register) has largely transitioned to CIMSPA. Many gyms prefer or require CIMSPA affiliation.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_T9A4zX": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What happens after I complete the course?",
            "row_content": "<p>You'll receive your certificate, be eligible for insurance/CIMSPA, and can start working immediately. StudyActive offers ongoing support: CPD resources, alumni network, job guidance, and access to further courses.</p><p><br/>Still have questions? Contact our team for personalised advice!<br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
